{"id": "12417", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=12417", "title": "Garden City (Kansas)", "text": "Garden City is a town in Western region of Kansas.\nGet in.\nAmtrak's daily Southwest Chief Chicago-Los Angeles line stops in Garden City. The westbound train arrives at 6:45AM and the eastbound train arrives at 11:35PM.\nGarden City is served by Bee Line Express. The station is at the Finney County Transit building (next to the Valero).\nGet around.\nThere is only one cab company in town.\nBy bus.\nFinney County Transit operates the City Link Bus Phone: +1 620 272-3626. Buses run between 6AM and 7PM, Monday through Friday. The fare is $1. A monthly pass is available for $30 from the transit office at 1008 N. Eleventh Street."}
{"id": "12418", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=12418", "title": "Garden City (Michigan)", "text": "Garden City is a city of 26,000 people (2016) in Wayne County in the state of Michigan. It is part of the Metro Detroit region and is approximately 10 miles (16.1 km) west of the city of Detroit. The city was patterned after the \"garden city\" concept that became popular in England during the 19th century, with most home sites sectioned off into 1-acre (4,000 m\u00b2) plots to allow adequate farming area to support the family with fruit and vegetables. Most sites are now considerably smaller, some as small as 40 feet by 135 feet.\nDo.\nGarden City is home to the world's first K-mart at 29600 Ford Rd."}
{"id": "12419", "revid": "2236161", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=12419", "title": "Garden City (South Carolina)", "text": "Garden City is a coastal city located in the Grand Strand region of South Carolina's northern coast."}
{"id": "12420", "revid": "2253620", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=12420", "title": "Garden City (Utah)", "text": "Garden City is a town in the Wasatch Range of Utah.\nUnderstand.\nGarden City is the largest town in Rich County with a population of just over 500. It sits on the shore of Bear Lake.\nGet in.\nDrive north on I-15 from Salt Lake City. Take exit 362 (Brigham City), and follow US 89/91 to Logan. Continue on US 89 to Garden City. It is about 2 and half hours away from Salt Lake City.\nGet around.\nA car will be needed to get around most of the time. There are bike rentals and many miles of trails.\nConnect.\nThe area code is 435"}
